can add new facts on appeal.

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.013
You can't.

00:13:12.013 --> 00:13:14.180
The appellate court, well,
at least generally speaking,

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:16.920
is not allowed to add new
facts into the record.

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:20.100
So this guy that's looking
away from deference

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:20.933
to the trial court,

00:13:20.933 --> 00:13:23.450
the appellate court is
supposed to give deference

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:25.560
to the trial court's factual findings,

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:29.050
and yet appellate courts
will often find some way

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:31.410
of bringing up a new fact into the record.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:32.390
They shouldn't do it.

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:34.030
It's not their job to do it.

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:35.560
